1. What you may do

   a) Download, install and run the Software, free of charge.
   b) Read and study the source code.
   c) Change the Software on your own computer for your own use, as long
      as you do not pass the changed version on.

2. Your own modules

   You may write and publish your own addons that work together with the
   Software while both are running (for example by listing ezCore as a
   dependency and calling its public functions), under any license you
   choose, provided that
   a) they contain no code, data or images taken from the Software, and
   b) they do not give the impression of being part of, or approved by,
      the ezCollection project.

3. Contributing

   a) You may copy ("fork") the repository for the sole purpose of
      preparing changes and offering them to the official ezCollection
      repository, for example as a pull request. Such a copy must not be
      published or passed on as a product of its own.
   b) When you offer a contribution (code, text, translations, images or
      collected game data), you grant the author a permanent, worldwide,
      free, irrevocable right to use, change, publish and pass on your
      contribution as part of the Software, under this or any later
      license of the Software. You confirm that you are allowed to grant
      this. You keep your own rights in what you contributed.

4. What you may not do

   Without written permission from the author you may not
   a) copy code, data or images of the Software, or parts of them, into
      other addons or other projects;
   b) publish, upload, mirror, repackage or otherwise pass on the
      Software or changed versions of it;
   c) sell the Software or charge for access to it;
   d) use the name "ezCollection" or its logo for other projects.

5. Ending

   These permissions end automatically if you break the terms above.

